	<x:String x:Key="SettingsAppearanceLead">Applies immediately, to every open tab.</x:String>
	<x:String x:Key="SettingsFollowSystemTitle">Follow the system theme</x:String>
	<x:String x:Key="SettingsFollowSystemDesc">Switch between light and dark along with the operating system. Turn this off to pick one yourself.</x:String>
	<x:String x:Key="SettingsDarkThemeTitle">Dark theme</x:String>
	<x:String x:Key="SettingsDarkThemeDesc">Available once the app is no longer following the system.</x:String>
	<x:String x:Key="SettingsLanguageTitle">Language</x:String>
	<x:String x:Key="SettingsLanguageDesc">Changes the interface language right away — no restart.</x:String>

	<x:String x:Key="SettingsNotificationsLead">Notifications are always kept in the bell panel; this only controls whether they also appear on screen.</x:String>
	<x:String x:Key="SettingsPopupsTitle">Show pop-up notifications</x:String>
	<x:String x:Key="SettingsPopupsDesc">Brief messages in the corner when something is imported, saved or fails. With this off, they go straight to the bell panel.</x:String>

	<x:String x:Key="SettingsEditorLead">Behaviour of the table and JSON editors.</x:String>
	<x:String x:Key="SettingsDiffOnSaveTitle">Show changes before saving</x:String>
	<x:String x:Key="SettingsDiffOnSaveDesc">Lists what is about to be written and asks for confirmation. This is the same switch as the "Don't show this again" box in that dialog.</x:String>


	<x:String x:Key="SettingsHelpLead">Links. The tour and the formula reference have their own buttons in the header, next to this one.</x:String>
	<x:String x:Key="SettingsReleases">Releases and changelog</x:String>

	<x:String x:Key="TourSettingsTitle">Settings</x:String>
	<x:String x:Key="TourSettingsText">Everything you set once and forget: theme, language, notifications, editor behaviour and comparison options. The About section has the version and the release list.</x:String>

	<x:String x:Key="TourHelpStepTitle">Replay this tour</x:String>
	<x:String x:Key="TourHelpStepText">This button brings the tour back whenever you want it.</x:String>
	<x:String x:Key="TourFormulaHelpBtnTitle">Formula reference</x:String>
	<x:String x:Key="TourFormulaHelpBtnText">Cells can compute themselves from other cells. This opens the reference: how to write a formula, how to address another row or a whole column, and every function with an example.</x:String>
